 Test_GETVideos_PresenterID_Inclusive←{
⍝ Test that ?presenter_id=3,4 returns videos with presenter 3 or 4, not only those with both
⍝ GenerateTestData fixes presenter 3 on presentations 3 and 4, presenter 4 on presentation 3 only,
⍝ so an AND filter would drop presentation 4's video from the result.
     H←##.##.##.HttpCommand
     Assert←##.Assert
     Videos←⍵∘{
         res←H.GetJSON'GET'(⍺,'/videos?per_page=1000&presenter_id=',⍵)
         'Expected 200 OK from /videos'Assert 200=res.HttpStatus:
         'Expected a paginated envelope from /videos'Assert~0∊⍴res.Data:
         res.Data.data
     }
     either←Videos'3,4'
     'Expected videos for presenters 3 or 4'Assert 0<≢either:
     'Every result must have presenter 3 or presenter 4'Assert ∧/∨⌿3 4∘.∊either.presenter_id:
⍝ The union, not the intersection: each presenter's own videos must all be present
     each←∪(Videos'3').youtube_id,(Videos'4').youtube_id
     'Results must include every video of presenter 3 and of presenter 4'Assert ∧/each∊either.youtube_id:
     1
 }
